        "answer": {
          "short": "French only: $5$; French and German: $10$; German only: $12$; neither: $3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}|F\\cup G|&=30-3=27\\\\|F\\cap G|&=15+22-27=10\\\\|F\\cap\\overline G|&=15-10=5\\\\|\\overline F\\cap G|&=22-10=12\\end{align*}$$\nPlace $5$, $10$ and $12$ in the French-only, intersection and German-only regions, respectively, and $3$ outside both circles.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p31-q7-a-solution-venn",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"teacher PDF page 76, printed page 654, question 7(a), p31-q7-a-solution-venn\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (0,0) rectangle (8,4);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (8,4);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (3,1.9) circle[radius=1.5];\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (5,1.9) circle[radius=1.5];\n\\node at (2.1,3.65) {French};\n\\node at (5.9,3.65) {German};\n\\node at (2,1.9) {$5$};\n\\node at (4,1.9) {$10$};\n\\node at (6,1.9) {$12$};\n\\node at (0.65,1.9) {$3$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
